  "description": "We are thinking we will have more Evasions in either November-ish, or the first couple months of 2027. We do not know what colors they will be\n\nThe Evasion, often imitated, never duplicated. The Satanic Rando. The DFL. The original Crust. Whatever you have or want to call it, its a bike that can fit a big ol' tire that doesn't ride like something that's been 6 feet under for that past 10 years. In terms of braze-ons the Evasion has everything you'd need to go for a tour around the world and back. If you're wondering which of our models is our go-to do-it-all bike, the Evasion is it.\n\nDon't forget to size up!\n\nDesigned around a 26x3\" wheel and tire combo and that's its max 26\" size. We've got 26x2.8\" WTB Rangers Here\n\nWord has it 26\" is dead (It Ain't. Don't Fear Opulence.) so you will likely go with a 27.5\" wheel. The max tire size there is going to be 27.5x2.8\".\n\nIt can be setup 29\", in which case your max tire size is going to be a 29x 2.0\".\n\nTakes a MOUNTAIN crank. Ideally 1x with a maximum ~40 tooth chainring. You can set it up 2x, but it's on you to figure that out.\n\nThe rocker dropout's adjustability means it is Rohloff and single speed compatible. If you're looking for a dedicated single speed hub the Paul Word Hub is a good option. If you want to run a Rohloff, it's recommended to swap to slotted dropouts opposed to the Thru Axle dropouts.\n\nFront brake is I.S. Mount and takes an adaptor to fit a caliper. The Rear brake is I.S. (Post Mount) as well, but you can bolt a caliper straight to the Rocker Dropout and clear a 160mm rotor. If you're struggling to find a brake setup, the Crust Palm Oil Brake Kit will help solve that problem.\n\nFront and rear thru axles are included.\n\nThe painted frames are all ED Coated to help protect it from the elements and inhibit internal corrosion. This doesn't mean you're free to ride it into the ocean though.\n\nTakes a 30.0mm seat post clamp with a 27.2 seat post.\n\nHeadset not included\n\nIf you need a seat post clamp we have some HERE!\n\nHandmade in Taiwan using Heat Treated Chromoly\n\nTig Welded",
